    rdfs:label "Evidence for Spices Cinnamon used in Pharmaceuticals & Druggists' Preparations: Mortimer (1823), General Commercial Dictionary, scan p. 113"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "Both those barks have nearly the same medicinal properties as cinnamon; they are however weaker, and do not possess any degree of astringency. Cinnamon, (GER. Zimmet, Kanehl."@en ;
